THOUGHT: `controllerChannel` is annotated `@Nullable`, but `init()` throws if it’s null, so after successful init it’s effectively non-null. NullAway still complains at the dereference in `update()`. The safest fix is to add a local non-null check (or assertion) in `update()` before dereferencing, which won’t change behavior because `init()` already guarantees non-null at runtime. I’ll modify the file to add a defensive null check and throw a `GdxRuntimeException` if `controllerChannel` is unexpectedly null, then later we can re-run the build. For now I’ll apply the code change.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '46,50c\  @Override
  public void update() {
    if (controllerChannel == null) {
      throw new GdxRuntimeException("ParticleController channel not initialized");
    }
    for (int i = 0, c = controller.particles.size; i < c; ++i) {
      controllerChannel.data[i].draw();
    }
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/particles/renderers/ParticleControllerControllerRenderer.java
```

